 <p>The independent QC table reports each untransfected stage’s first, mean and median RFU, plus the median across the twelve wells of response-mean / paired-baseline-mean ratios. These formulas are explicit. The original QC field named <code>median_col12_F0a</code> equals the first reading in each row; its published ratio algorithm is unspecified. The original table is retained for audit, not silently relabeled.</p>
 <p>All 96 well summaries retain unmasked arithmetic in clearly labeled <code>*_computed</code> columns. The <code>*_retained</code> columns leave excluded values empty, never zero. The source’s VUAA1 normalization is not used: it includes a negative Or7a denominator and otherwise depends on single, unvalidated reference wells. The recalculated six-well 3 SD value is an audit of the source report only; it is not a limit of detection or a response cutoff. No technical-read error bars, confidence intervals or p values are used to imply biological replication.</p>
 <h4 class="reading-heading--detail">Acquisition limits</h4><p>Numeric gains, final VOC concentrations, exact addition delays and a matched DMSO-only condition are unavailable. The source records partial detachment without quantifying it. Test 1 contains one well per condition × stimulus and no independent culture repeats; <a href="results.html#limitations">Results</a> explains the consequences for interpretation.</p>
-<p class="exp-see-also"><a href="results.html#kinetic-pilot">Read the Test 1 result →</a> · <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/downloads/b826bffef90c-plate-p2-methods.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer">Test 1 executed methods · PDF</a></p><h3 id="exp-test2-kinetics">Test 2: two-acquisition odor panel</h3><p>Test 2 contains 72 wells and 1,440 readings. Rows A, D, E, F, G and H contain VUAA1, isopentyl acetate, 2-heptanone, valeric acid, pentyl acetate and DMSO control, respectively. VUAA1 was diluted 1:100; the odor solutions were diluted 1:1,000, with 0.1% DMSO reported. Stock concentrations were not supplied.</p><p>Positions 1–12 are Or7a + ORCO, Or19a + ORCO, Or42a + ORCO, Or98a + ORCO, Or22a + ORCO, Or67a + ORCO, Or67b + ORCO, Or59b + ORCO, Or85b + ORCO, Or35a + ORCO, ORCO only and blank. F0 contains five reads over 0–48 s; F1 contains fifteen reads over 0–168 s, both at 12 s intervals. Each acquisition starts its own clock. <a href="results.html#vuaa1-reference-method">Results defines the endpoint correction and VUAA1-reference normalization.</a></p></section><section class="section-block exp-proto" data-protocol-id="stable-selection" data-reveal="" id="stable-selection">
+<p class="exp-see-also"><a href="results.html#kinetic-pilot">Read the Test 1 result →</a> · <a href="https://static.igem.wiki/teams/6460/wiki/downloads/b826bffef90c-plate-p2-methods.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer">Test 1 executed methods · PDF</a></p><h3 id="exp-test2-kinetics">Test 2: two-acquisition odor panel</h3><p>Test 2 contains 72 wells and 1,440 readings. Rows A, D, E, F, G and H contain VUAA1, isopentyl acetate, 2-heptanone, valeric acid, pentyl acetate and DMSO control, respectively. VUAA1 was diluted 1:100; the odor solutions were diluted 1:1,000, with 0.1% DMSO reported. Stock concentrations were not supplied.</p><p>Positions 1–12 are Or7a + ORCO, Or19a + ORCO, Or42a + ORCO, Or98a + ORCO, Or22a + ORCO, Or67a + ORCO, Or67b + ORCO, Or59b + ORCO, Or85b + ORCO, Or35a + ORCO, ORCO only and blank. F0 contains five reads over 0–48 s; F1 contains fifteen reads over 0–168 s, both at 12 s intervals. Each acquisition starts its own clock. <a href="results.html#vuaa1-reference-method">Results defines the endpoint correction and VUAA1-reference normalization.</a></p><div id="exp-f1-dynamic"><h3 class="reading-heading--topic"><dfn title="Post-addition fluorescence acquisition">F1</dfn>-only dynamic reanalysis</h3><p>The supplied <dfn title="Post-addition fluorescence acquisition">F1</dfn> workbook retains 1,080 readings: six conditions × twelve channels × fifteen readings, at 12 s intervals from 0 to 168 s. For each well, E is the mean at 0, 12 and 24 s and L is the mean at 144, 156 and 168 s. D = L/E − 1; the vehicle-referenced contrast is C = D<sub>odor</sub> − D<sub>DMSO</sub> for the same channel. We report 100C in percentage points. F0 does not enter this calculation; VUAA1 remains a reference record and is not a denominator or exclusion criterion.</p><p>The delivered channel order is Or7a, Or19a, Or42a, Or98a, Or22a, Or67a, Or67b, Or59b, Or85b, Or35a, ORCO only and blank. Analysis follows the workbook’s channel labels and source-cell provenance. DMSO fraction and addition volume were matched as confirmed by the experimenter. Pearson and Spearman correlations are calculated separately for each odorant across the ten tuning ORs, using DoOR consensus minus each receptor’s spontaneous firing rate. The missing Or42a–valeric acid reference is omitted from that correlation only. Controls are retained separately, and all signed contrasts are preserved. <a href="https://gitlab.igem.org/2026/software/nthu/aerosense/-/tree/main/code/aerosense/wetlab/odor-f1-dynamic">Reproduction and validation code</a> · <a href="results.html#f1-dynamic-door">Results</a>.</p></div></section><section class="section-block exp-proto" data-protocol-id="stable-selection" data-reveal="" id="stable-selection">
